    faqs: [
      { question: 'What is the most common mistake in animal walk cycles?', answer: 'Treating the animal like two human walks stuck together. The front and rear leg pairs must synchronize with spinal flexion and scapular sliding.' }, 
      {"question":"How should an animator study Quadruped & Animal Walk Cycle Animation Reference frame by frame?","answer":"Step through the footage using arrow keys to pinpoint contact and reversal frames. Map out the line of action and pelvis trajectory first before keyframing limb details, and test your timing with side-by-side playblast comparison."}],
